# DESCRIPTION

A setting is a typed attribute on a file in `/data/Settings` on Taisce's volume (fs(4)), one file an area (`Appearance`, `Keyboard`, `Mouse`, `Deskbar`, `Grants`, `Recent`) and each attribute named `Area:Name` (`Keyboard:RepeatDelay`).
There is no settings service and no configuration language: a program reads an area's attributes with `NodeClient.stat` and writes one with `FsIPC.FileClient.setAttribute`, and `rc`'s `attr` builtin (rc(1)) reads, sets, lists and removes the same attributes from the shell.
Settings is tier 0, so a service links it as an app does.

`value` reads a `Setting`'s attribute from `/data/Settings/AREA` and passes it through `accept`, which gives the setting's `fallback` when the file or the attribute is absent, holds another type, is outside `range` or is not in `choices`.
`set` makes `/data/Settings` and the area's file if they are not there yet, then writes the accepted value's attribute.
`read` returns every int64, bool and string attribute on `/data/Settings/AREA`.

`watch` makes `/data/Settings` if need be and opens a Node watch (`NodeIPC.NodeClient.watch`, node(5)) on the folder.
Because Taisce records a file's creation, removal and attribute changes as directory changes on its parent — with `name` as `"Area"` when the file is made or removed and `"Area:Name"` when an attribute `Area:Name` on `Area` is set or removed — one watch on `/data/Settings` hears every setting and grant change.
`touches` says whether a `NodeIPC.Change` is for `area` (`"Area"`, `"Area:..."`, or an overflow).

`Grants` records the answers a user asked the trusted prompt to remember (`allow for this app`), as boolean attributes on `/data/Settings/Grants` named `Grants:APP.SERVICE` (`Grants:tile.shortcuts = true`).
`recorded` reads one (`nil` when none is recorded, `true` when allowed, `false` when denied), `record` writes one, `list` returns every boolean `Grants:APP.SERVICE` attribute on `/data/Settings/Grants` in attribute order, and `revoke` removes the attribute with `FsIPC.FileClient.removeAttribute` (`attr -d /data/Settings/Grants Grants:APP.SERVICE` in `rc`), waking any watch on `/data/Settings`.

`Recent` keeps the last `kept` (10) documents (`Recent:Documents`), folders (`Recent:Folders`) and apps (`Recent:Apps`) opened, newest first, each a newline-separated string attribute on `/data/Settings/Recent`.
`note` puts `item` at the front of `name`, dropping any earlier occurrence and trimming the list to `kept`.

# EXAMPLES

Read and change a setting or a recorded grant from `rc`(1):

```rc
% attr /data/Settings/Keyboard Keyboard:RepeatDelay 250
% attr /data/Settings/Keyboard Keyboard:RepeatDelay
250
% attr /data/Settings/Grants
Grants:tile.shortcuts true
% attr -d /data/Settings/Grants Grants:tile.shortcuts
```

# FILES

: `/data/Settings`
  The directory of setting areas on the Taisce volume.
: `/data/Settings/Appearance`, `/data/Settings/Keyboard`, `/data/Settings/Mouse`, `/data/Settings/Deskbar`
  Area files whose typed attributes hold the desktop's settings.
: `/data/Settings/Grants`
  Recorded permission grants, one boolean attribute (`Grants:APP.SERVICE`) each.
: `/data/Settings/Recent`
  Recent documents, folders and apps, as string attributes (`Recent:Documents`, `Recent:Folders`, `Recent:Apps`), a line an item, newest first.

